# Design System & Visual Identity

## Design Philosophy

FlexYug is a **calm, minimal workout journal**. Every design decision follows this priority order; never invert it:

1. **Clarity**: the user should instantly understand what they're looking at
2. **Usability**: every interaction should feel obvious and forgiving
3. **Speed**: perceived and actual; no layout jank, no unnecessary spinners
4. **Consistency**: identical patterns for identical actions, everywhere
5. **Delight**: subtle motion and refined details, earned only after the above are satisfied

### Foundational Principles

**Dieter Rams: remove everything unnecessary.** Fewer buttons, fewer visual elements, more whitespace. If an element doesn't serve the user's current task, it shouldn't be on screen.

**Don Norman: match human mental models.** Behavior must be predictable. Labels must be clear. Actions must be obvious.

**Apple Health aesthetic.** Restrained, typographic, spacious; not typical fitness-app design. Inspirations: Apple Health, Apple Fitness, Whoop, Strava, Strong, Hevy.

### Non-negotiables

- **Single column**, phone-first; no tablet-specific layouts
- **Brutalist-lifter palette + curated skins**: four skins (`forge`, `iron`, `ember`, `chalk`) in `src/ui/skins.ts`, each a coordinated `{ dark, light }` pair selected by system color scheme. Default is Forge: muted green accent on near-black (dark) or warm paper (light). Switchable in Profile → Appearance.
- **Geist fonts**: Geist Sans for chrome/labels, Geist Mono for numerals and data, loaded via `@expo-google-fonts/geist` + `geist-mono`. Render text through the `<Text variant>` primitive in `src/ui/Text.tsx` so no screen falls back to the system font.
- **44pt minimum touch target** (`theme.touch.min`) on every interactive element
- **Generous whitespace**: when in doubt, add more
- **Subtle motion** only: 150 / 220 / 320 ms duration tokens plus a 600ms counter tally (`theme.motion.duration`), and three damped Reanimated springs (`snappy` / `settle` / `rebound`). No particles, no parallax.
- **Progressive disclosure**: primary action visible; secondary actions revealed on interaction

## Styling Rules

Tokens live in the modules under `src/ui/`: `colors.ts` / `skins.ts` (palette), `typography.ts`, `motion.ts`, plus the `space` / `radius` / `touch` scales in `useTheme.ts`. Consume them through the `useTheme()` hook with a memoized `makeStyles(theme)` factory. The legacy static `src/ui/theme.ts` is a deprecated shim kept only for the pre-hydration boot overlay and the `brand` constants; do not use it in new code. There are **no CSS files in the mobile app**.

### Always use tokens

```tsx
// Correct
import { useMemo } from 'react';
import { StyleSheet, View } from 'react-native';

import { Text } from '@/ui/Text';
import { useTheme, type Theme } from '@/ui/useTheme';

export function Card({ title }: { title: string }) {
  const theme = useTheme();
  const styles = useMemo(() => makeStyles(theme), [theme]);
  return (
    <View style={styles.card}>
      <Text variant="card">{title}</Text>
    </View>
  );
}

const makeStyles = (theme: Theme) =>
  StyleSheet.create({
    card: {
      padding: theme.space.s4,
      backgroundColor: theme.color.surface,
      borderRadius: theme.radius.md,
    },
  });
```

```ts
// Wrong: hard-coded values, static theme shim
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: { padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#FFFFFF', borderRadius: 12 },
});
```

### Token surface (via `useTheme()`)

| Category | Tokens                                                                                                  |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Color    | `bg`, `surface`, `surface2`, `border`, `borderStrong`, `ink`, `inkSecondary`, `inkTertiary`, `inkHero`, `accent`, `accentSoft`, `success`, `successSoft`, `danger`, `dangerSoft`, `onAccent`, `overlay` |
| Space    | `half` (2), `s1` (4) → `s12` (48), `page` (20), `section` (32)                                          |
| Radius   | `sm` (8), `md` (12), `lg` (16), `full` (9999), `card` (14), `button` (8)                                |
| Font     | `size.hero/display/title/card/body/meta/micro`; `family.sans/sansMedium/sansSemibold/mono/monoMedium`; `weight.regular/medium/semibold` (there is no 700) |
| Touch    | `min` (44), `navHeight` (64), `cta` (52), `avatar` (56), `avatarRadius` (28)                            |
| Motion   | `duration.fast` (150), `duration.base` (220), `duration.slow` (320), `duration.counter` (600); `spring.snappy/settle/rebound` |

## Components and Interactions

### Pressables

Use `Pressable` for everything interactive. Express pressed state via a function style prop:

```tsx
<Pressable
  onPress={onStart}
  style={({ pressed }) => [styles.cta, pressed && styles.ctaPressed]}
>
  <Text variant="card" color={theme.color.onAccent}>Start workout</Text>
</Pressable>
```

Keep the pressed effect subtle: a lighter background or `opacity: 0.9`. No scale-on-press bounces.

### Feedback

- Haptics via the wrappers in `src/ui/haptics.ts`; never call `expo-haptics` directly. Trigger map: `haptics.light` (stepper increments, sheet actions, skip-rest), `haptics.medium` (set banked / last set of exercise), `haptics.rigid` (swipe crosses completion threshold), `haptics.success` (rest timer hits target, PR achieved)
- Background rest cue via the local notification in `src/lib/restNotifications.ts`
- Toasts via `ToastProvider` (`useToast()` from `src/ui/ToastContext.tsx`); do NOT use `Alert.alert` for transient feedback

### Charts

Charts are in-house SVG. Use `src/ui/LineChart.tsx` or extend it; do not add Recharts or `victory-native`. Axes, ticks, and labels use `theme.color.inkTertiary`.

### Icons

SVG icons via `react-native-svg`, centralized in `src/ui/TabIcon.tsx` and similar components. No icon libraries with per-glyph imports (no `@expo/vector-icons` sprawl).

## Layout Defaults

- Screens: `SafeAreaView` → `ScrollView` with `contentContainerStyle: { padding: theme.space.page, gap: theme.space.s4 }`
- Cards: `backgroundColor: theme.color.surface`, `borderRadius: theme.radius.md`, `borderWidth: 1`, `borderColor: theme.color.border`, `padding: theme.space.s4`
- Primary CTA: `backgroundColor: theme.color.accent`, `color: theme.color.onAccent`, `height: 52`, `borderRadius: theme.radius.md`

## Responsive

Phone-first. No media queries, no `Dimensions`-based layout branching unless strictly needed. Keep everything single-column and let `flex` handle the rest.

## Grandfathered Exceptions

Short prefixes on legacy components (`hd-`, `pg-`, `esm-`) existed only in the old CSS world and do not apply to the RN codebase. Use descriptive component and style names everywhere.
